The design choice for the Google Sheet follows a **"One Row per Item"** structure (also known as Tidy Data). This is the professional way to handle forms with multiple entries.

### How it works:
If you submit a form with **2 Travel items** and **1 Food item**:
*   The script will create **3 separate rows** in your sheet.
*   All 3 rows will have the **same Submission ID**, so you know they belong to the same person and same claim.
*   For **Food, Accommodation, and Other**: The "From Location" and "To Location" columns will simply show a **"-"**, while the Date, Amount, and Attachment columns will save the specific data for those items.

### Final Google Sheet Column Names (Header Row):
Ensure Row 1 of your sheet looks exactly like this:

| Column | Header Name | Description |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **A** | **Timestamp** | Submission time |
| **B** | **Submission ID** | Group ID for all items in one form |
| **C** | **Branch Name** | Mumbai, Delhi, etc. |
| **D** | **Salesperson Name** | Name selected |
| **E** | **Expense Category** | TRAVEL, FOOD, ACCOMMODATION, or OTHER |
